From: Chipyard Linux Bringup
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] mmc: sdhci-pltfm: allow optional IRQ for polling mode

On SoCs where the SDHCI controller interrupt is not routed to the
CPU's interrupt controller (e.g. RISC-V PL with PS peripherals
behind an AXI bridge), the platform_get_irq() call fails and
prevents the driver from probing at all.

Mark the IRQ as optional: when it is not available, set host->irq = 0.
The companion sdhci core patch adds a polling timer for this case.

Signed-off-by: Chipyard Linux Bringup

---
 drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pltfm.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pltfm.c b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pltfm.c
index xxxx..yyyy 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pltfm.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pltfm.c
@@ -123,9 +123,12 @@ struct sdhci_host *sdhci_pltfm_init(struct platform_device *pdev,
 		goto err;
 	}
 
-	irq = platform_get_irq(pdev, 0);
+	irq = platform_get_irq_optional(pdev, 0);
 	if (irq < 0) {
-		ret = irq;
+		dev_info(&pdev->dev,
+			 "no IRQ found, will use polling mode\n");
+		irq = 0;
+	}
-		goto err;
 	}
 
 	host = sdhci_alloc_host(&pdev->dev,
